            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for the way something is done, then the Mandarin for to argue in favour of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: shìshí",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shìshí — \"fact\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ juéde tā shuō de shì shìshí — I think what he says is true."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shìshí is built from 事 'a matter' and shí, both inherited from Middle Chinese, dzriH and zyit (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'full' and 'sincere'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons."
